86455882765586e-06,-0.10528063029050827,-4.2676016164477915e-05,-1.4305104514278355e-06,-1.1920928244535389e-07,-0.00010191874753218144,-0.15226826071739197,-2.9802276912960224e-06,-2.8371408916427754e-05,-1.3947389561508317e-05,-2.4676019165781327e-05,-0.021986311301589012,-0.11630045622587204,-6.6756979322235566e-06,-8.344646857949556e-07,-4.4225667807040736e-05,-3.576278118089249e-07,-1.1920928244535389e-07,-0.00019536493346095085,-1.6458768844604492,0.0,0.0,-0.00029273517429828644,-1.1920928244535389e-07,-0.0020553194917738438,0.0,-0.015528248623013496,-0.10967197269201279,-0.0002273062855238095,-2.3841855067985307e-07,-7.188061863416806e-05,-3.528532761265524e-05,-2.145764938177308e-06,0.0,-0.00011193125828867778,-2.622600959512056e-06,-2.622600959512056e-06],"request":{"active_prefix":"","input_ids":[151644,8948,198,2610,525,1207,16948,11,3465,553,54364,14817,13,1446,525,264,10950,17847,13,151645,198,151644,872,198,50,3948,279,3491,3019,553,3019,13,20678,697,1590,4226,304,1124,79075,90,1112,92,382,9885,279,2629,315,279,9904,311,198,78045,17,1124,15940,61,18,856,481,220,18,1124,15940,856,284,481,59,37018,90,18,15170,17,92,1124,15940,220,17,87,59,60,258,279,9873,400,15,1124,273,856,1124,273,220,17,1124,2493,2418,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nFind the sum of the solutions to\n\\[2 \\sin^3 x - 3 \\sin x = -\\frac{3}{2} \\sin 2x\\]in the interval $0 \\le x \\le 2 \\pi.$","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"d50fb52595b342df7bd590fe9bef5cf82357be1e6cb2f0131665e44e20b85987"},"seconds":61.657716512680054,"seed":790667770003071814,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve the equation \\(2 \\sin^3 x - 3 \\sin x = -\\frac{3}{2} \\sin 2x\\) in the interval \\(0 \\le x \\le 2\\pi\\), we will follow these steps:\n\n1. **Simplify the equation by using trigonometric identities:**\n\n   Recall that \\(\\sin 2x = 2 \\sin x \\cos x\\). Substitute this into the equation:\n   \\[\n   2 \\sin^3 x - 3 \\sin x = -\\frac{3}{2} \\cdot 2 \\sin x \\cos x\n   \\]\n   Simplify the right-hand side:\n   \\[\n   2 \\sin^3 x - 3 \\sin x = -3 \\sin x \\cos x\n   \\]\n\n2. **Factor out \\(\\sin x\\) from both sides of the equation:**\n\n   \\[\n   \\sin x (2 \\sin^2 x - 3) = -3 \\sin x \\cos x\n   \\]\n\n3. **Consider the case when \\(\\sin x = 0\\):**\n\n   If \\(\\sin x = 0\\), then \\(x = 0, \\pi, 2\\pi\\) in the interval \\(0 \\le x \\le 2\\pi\\).\n\n4. **For \\(\\sin x \\neq 0\\), divide both sides by \\(\\sin x\\):**\n\n   \\[\n   2 \\sin^2 x - 3 = -3 \\cos x\n   \\]\n\n5. **Rearrange the equation to isolate \\(\\cos x\\):**\n\n   \\[\n   2 \\sin^2 x + 3 \\cos x - 3 = 0\n   \\]\n\n6. **Use the Pythagorean identity \\(\\sin^2 x = 1 - \\cos^2 x\\):**\n\n   Substitute \\(\\sin^2 x\\) with \\(1 - \\cos^2 x\\):\n   \\[\n   2 (1 - \\cos^2 x) + 3 \\cos x - 3 = 0\n   \\]\n   Simplify the equation:\n   \\[\n   2 - 2 \\cos^2 x + 3 \\cos x - 3 = 0\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   -2 \\cos^2 x + 3 \\cos x - 1 = 0\n   \\]\n   Multiply through by \\(-1\\) for simplicity:\n   \\[\n   2 \\cos^2 x - 3 \\cos x + 1 = 0\n   \\]\n\n7. **Solve the quadratic equation \\(2 \\cos^2 x - 3 \\cos x + 1 = 0\\):**\n\n   Use the quadratic formula \\(y = \\cos x\\):\n   \\[\n   y = \\frac{-b \\pm \\sqrt{b^2 - 4ac}}{2a}\n   \\]\n   Here, \\(a = 2\\), \\(b = -3\\), and \\(c = 1\\):\n   \\[\n   y = \\frac{3 \\pm \\sqrt{9 - 8}}{4} = \\frac{3 \\pm 1}{4}\n   \\]\n   This gives us two solutions:\n   \\[\n   y = \\frac{4}{4} = 1 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad y = \\frac{2}{4} = \\frac{1}{2}\n   \\]\n\n8. **Find the corresponding values of \\(x\\) for \\(\\cos x = 1\\) and \\(\\cos x = \\frac{1}{2}\\):**\n\n   - For \\(\\cos x = 1\\):\n     \\[\n     x = 0\n     \\]\n   - For \\(\\cos x = \\frac{1}{2}\\):\n     \\[\n     x = \\frac{\\pi}{3}, \\frac{5\\pi}{3}\n     \\]\n\n9. **Combine all solutions:**\n\n   The solutions are \\(x = 0, \\pi, 2\\pi, \\frac{\\pi}{3}, \\frac{5\\pi}{3}\\).\n\n10. **Sum the solutions:**\n\n   \\[\n   0 + \\pi + 2\\pi + \\frac{\\pi}{3} + \\frac{5\\pi}{3} = \\pi + 2\\pi + \\frac{\\pi + 5\\pi}{3} = 3\\pi + 2\\pi = 5\\pi\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the sum of the solutions is \\(\\boxed{5\\pi}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{5\\pi}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
